 "script": [
  {"id": "hook", "text": "Istanbul just saw its heaviest rainfall since records began. How bad did it get?"},
  {"id": "f1", "text": "Istanbul's governor, Davut Gül, said Wednesday's rain was the highest since records began in 1942. Schools were closed, and the governor later said they would stay shut until Monday. Motorcycles were banned from the roads that evening."},
  {"id": "f2", "text": "Turkey's disaster agency, AFAD, had logged one thousand two hundred seventy-seven flooding incidents, fifteen landslides, and forty-seven stranded people by Wednesday night. About eight thousand personnel were deployed, Daily Sabah reported."},
  {"id": "f3", "text": "Euronews and Al Jazeera report at least two deaths, including a fourteen-year-old boy electrocuted in the Balat district. In Sultangazi, a school's retaining wall collapsed with students inside. No injuries were reported there. Counts differ between outlets, so the toll may change."},
  {"id": "cta", "text": "Will Istanbul face another flood this autumn? Yes or no?"}
 ],
